use ../../../lib/UiComponent

from ../../../behaviors/FormParticipation import FormParticipation
from ../../buttons/Button import Button

export ui-component SignaturePad:
    description:
        A signature pad is an area where the user draws their signature with a
        finger, pen, or mouse. The drawing is its value, and the user can clear
        it and start again.

    composes:
        - @{Button}

    behaviors:
        - @{FormParticipation}

    drawing:
        Pressing and moving draws a line that follows the pointer, and letting
        go ends it. A signature can be made of many lines. Lines are smoothed,
        and can vary in thickness with the pen's pressure or the speed of
        drawing, like ink. While drawing, the page doesn't scroll and no text
        is selected.

    ink:
        The component sets the colour and thickness of the lines.

    clearing:
        A clear Button removes the whole drawing. Whether the last line can be
        undone on its own is up to the chosen library.

    value:
        The value is the lines drawn, and it is empty until something is drawn.
        The component using the pad is told as each line is drawn and when it
        is finished, and can get the drawing as an image. It can also set the
        lines itself, such as to show a signature saved earlier.

    form:
        In a form, the component decides what is sent for the drawing, such as
        the image. A required pad with nothing drawn counts as empty.

    guide:
        The pad can show a line to sign on and a hint such as "Sign here".
        These are not part of the drawing.

    disabled:
        A disabled pad can't be drawn on or cleared. A read-only pad shows its
        drawing but can't be changed.

    otherWays:
        A signature can't be drawn with the keyboard, and some users can't
        draw one at all. The pad has a name that assistive tools read out, and
        says whether anything has been drawn. Wherever a signature is asked
        for, the app offers another way to give one, such as typing a name.

    nonGoals:
        - It doesn't check that a signature is genuine, or who drew it
        - Not a drawing tool. No colours to pick, rubbing out, or shapes
